        "name":  "create_topdown_tileset",
        "description":  "Generate a Wang tileset for top-down game maps with corner-based autotiling.\n\nThis tool starts an asynchronous tileset generation that returns immediately with a tileset ID.\nUse get_topdown_tileset to check status and retrieve the completed tileset.\n\nCost: standard mode is 1-4 generations, usually 3 or 4 â NOT 1. (Measured\nover 6,124 prod charges: mean 3.1, only 4% cost exactly 1.) mode=\"pro\" costs\n15 generations for tiles up to 32 px, 25 above. Budget accordingly; six\nstandard tilesets is ~18 generations, not 6. Failed jobs are not charged.\n\nTile count depends on mode and transition depth:\n  - standard mode: 0.0 / 0.25 / 0.5 â 16 tiles (4x4); 1.0 â 25 tiles (4x8)\n  - pro mode:      0.0 / 0.25       â 16 tiles;        0.5 / 1.0 â 25 tiles\n  - shape_style:   0.0 through 0.5   â 16 tiles;       \u003e0.5 â 25 tiles\n(pro promotes 0.5 past the 0.4 threshold, so a pro request at 0.5 returns 25,\nnot 16.) The 25-tile layout has 21 distinct corner combos â the 4 extra\nwall-continuation tiles share corners with a twin and are distinguished by\npattern_4x4, not corners.\nVertices define terrain, tiles render based on their 4 corner values.\n\nUse case: Building top-down game maps with seamless terrain transitions.\n\nAlgorithm: For each grid cell, sample terrain at 4 vertices, select matching tile.\n\n## Creating Connected Tilesets\n\nUse base tile IDs to create multiple tilesets that seamlessly connect:\n\n1. Create first tileset (e.g., oceanâbeach) and wait for completion\n2. Use get_topdown_tileset to retrieve the base tile IDs\n3. Use the beach base tile ID as lower_base_tile_id for next tileset (beachâgrass)\n\nExample workflow:\n- Tileset 1: ocean (lower) â beach (upper) â get beach base tile ID\n- Tileset 2: beach (lower, using base tile ID) â grass (upper) â get grass base tile ID\n- Tileset 3: grass (lower, using base tile ID) â stone (upper)\n\nThis ensures visual consistency across terrain transitions.\n\nGeneration time: ~100 seconds (async processing)",
